[Music]  hello there  the best things in life are free well  that's what they say anyway  free to play games have become an  integral part of gaming culture  and are growing to the size of many aaa  games thanks to their focus on micro  in this series i outlined the last 10  free games you may have missed  and also bring your attention to older  free-to-play games that have had  an overhaul this is the 10th episode in  this series which started back in 2017  so if you don't see a game worth your  time in this video there's another 90 to  choose from in the playlist  always keep in mind all three games want  your money somehow but only you can  decide if they're worth it  enough jibber jabber let's go  our first game today a game centered  around the world of assassination  hitman 3. if you've ever looked at  hitman and wondered if slow paced  methodical manslaying is your type of  thing  well now you can try before you buy the  free starter pack has rotating content  first the training missions in which 47  aka the bald dude with a barcode  learns the tools of the trade and finds  out firsthand the difference between  going in guns blazing  or waiting for the right time to make  his handiwork look like a mere accident  the best thing about the hitman 3  starter pack is the free content  added monthly sometimes it will be a  full location with multiple targets to  subdue  other times it will be an elusive target  a game mode which only allows  one playthrough to ramp up the tension  of course they want you to buy the full  game  but there's no harm in taking advantage  of the ever-changing free content  and all progress carries over if you do  decide to spend your real-life cash  next we have vigger a totally  free-to-play survival looter shooter  set in norway vigor does some great  things to distance itself from its  rivals  firstly in this post-apocalyptic world  staying alive is vital  players move into an area and scavenge  for everything they can  supplies ammo and ultimately new weapons  then a slow-moving toxic cloud fills the  map and only certain paths  lead to your escape sounds easy right  well if you die  you lose everything that is on your  character  everything even that new shotgun you  just found  survival is key by taking the loot back  home it becomes safe  until you choose to take it back into  the fight other players will be under  the same pressure of risk reward  and should you all stay in game long  enough a monumental supply drop will  land  and all players will be alerted how far  do you push it  to be victorious fyi vigor uses battle  passes cosmetic items and weapon  blueprints  as the main avenue to making money when  was the last time you played chess  now's the time to return this is auto  chess just like the name suggests auto  chess is a strategy game with some  features like chess  but in reality it's closer to a tower  defense game  and a battle royale game we select our  heroes put them on the battlefield and  watch them smash 10 bells out of each  other until one team is victorious  each hero has stats and once on the  board we are helpless  hence why it's called auto chess this is  an automatic battle  characters are decided before the match  in a random fashion  thus making sure nobody has an unfair  advantage  at least at a base level as we all  attempt to collect the 70 heroes  auto chess is available on ps4 and now  has a ps5 version too  the game makes money via in-game  currency called donuts  and of course loot boxes too back in  late 2020  zelda breath of the wild released on  playstation sorry i read that wrong  gunshin impact arrived a totally  free-to-play role-playing game  which takes the backbone of that  nintendo game and monetizes it with  gacha style mechanics  the thing is this is way more than a  simple copy paste  genting impact is a triple a game in  everything but price  we are set free in a fully open world  with enemy tears to grind towards  exploration plays an important part but  it's the combat that really stands out  each character has their own magical  ability like an element  for example fire and ice each element is  strong against another but weak  against others giving it a kind of  rock-paper-scissors style decision  making to be made mid-fight  the fantasy story is surprisingly  compelling and the artwork and  soundtrack is simply mesmerizing  the game takes your cash via a surprise  random loot box mechanic  which can unlock some awe-inspiring  heroes with elemental abilities like no  others  i played for a while and i've got to  admit the gacha thing  is a little too addicting so keep that  in mind if you have that type of  mentality  don't get addicted  [Music]  next the first ever game on the list  which is ps5  only it's a sad day for ps4 this is  enlisted  a world war ii shooter enlisted looks  like the run-of-the-mill military  shoot-a-thon right  well it has a very impressive gimmick  instead of 150 players in a game at once  enlisted drastically brings down that  number and gives each player a platoon  to look after instead  a squad of four players are controlled  by one person  i know it sounds insane give me a sec to  explain we choose one of the squad  and the ai takes over the rest each of  the squad is a different class which we  can switch to on the fly  if one person falls in battle we are  instantly transported to another squad  mate  instead of respawning outside of combat  this makes fights much more personal and  long-winded  and it's a clever premise i recommend  you give it a try at least  enlisted wants your money through  in-game gold purchases  of different squads from history with  different weapon sets  next up we have rogue company i spoke  about this last time we met up and now  it's fully free to play  rogue company is a team shooter a squad  of players group up on a futuristic  chopper then skydive onto the  battlefield  to either frag out or secure points each  round we start back on that helicarrier  again  and use the blood money from the  previous fight to buy new weapons  rinse and repeat the best part are the  characters  each has a set of abilities and weapons  to choose from from a katana throwing  femme fatale  to a thanos snapping lone wolf who can  see enemies through walls for a few  seconds  each season a new character is released  and the makers hope you buy it with  in-game credits  but it's also possible to do this via  grinding daily bounties  the new ps5 version is out now with 120  frames per second and the ps4 version  runs surprisingly well too  i like roko i hope you do too and  because i like roko so much i wanted to  double back  on another free-to-play game from a few  years ago apex legends  i know you've tried it and i know you  either love it or you've left it behind  by now  well with season nine comes a new game  mode you should try  arena it's essentially the same as rogue  company but in first person  and with only three players per side  this game mode is a fantastic way to try  out new weapons outside of battle royale  arena is a permanent mode so grab a few  friends and jump in  it's a great break from battle royale  and on console at least  it's the closest we have to play  valorent for a while yet  [Music]  anyone into mumbai foreign massively  multiplayer online roleplaying games  mmorpgs have you tried bless unleashed  bless takes the usual formula of  journeying across the land facing lethal  monsters and feral beasts  in a tale of betrayal we build a team of  allies and take back  our lands the classes make up the bulk  of the gameplay loop with differing  skills  talents and fighting styles berserkers  are fearless warriors crusaders are a  little more tanky  mages wield magic and rangers like to  keep their distance like a glass cannon  from afar  find your playstyle meet up with some  friends and take on a god or two bless  unleashed uses booster packs and buffs  to take your money from your pocket and  there's some damn good cosmetics too  next we have a final fantasy game it's  called final fantasy crystal chronicles  remastered edition  light a seven word title wow as the name  suggests  this is not a full game but rather a  snippet as a way to entice you into  buying the full game  by the way the full game is actually  pretty cheap crystal chronicles is the  lost sheep in the final fantasy series  which has always  seemed to stand alone an rpg which  focuses on playing alongside your  friends in a squad  just like bless unleashed the core loop  is down to the class you choose  with cross play set up right away to  play alongside those who have the full  game  and those on other platforms too at  present three dungeons are available to  light players but if they have a person  with the full game in their crew  another 10 dungeons are available too  [Music]  okay so we've done nine and i struggled  to pick a number 10. so here's  two games instead battle operation 2  mobile suit gundam  sees you pilot a mech in a team focused  tactical shooter  it's just had a ps5 update and now has  english voiceovers  and crazy fast loading times and finally  love live school idol festival after  school activity way way home meeting  i can't believe that's one title a  rhythm game to rock out to your favorite  japanese tracks  to dancing girls huh you do you i guess  so that's it everyone is anybody  actually still here at the end of this  video  i'm totally on my own right now oh well  that's 10 more games that are free on  ps4 and ps5 ps5  and ps5 right now i'll check back with  you in six months with part 11.  this is a long-running series see ya

